# infra-change-review

Run against the branch diff:
`git diff {{ project.default_branch }}...HEAD -- {{ infra.iac_dir }}/ {{ infra.k8s_dir }}/ .github/workflows/ '*Dockerfile*'`

Work through each section that has changed files. Mark every item ✅ pass / ❌ fail / ⏭ n/a (with a reason).
Every ❌ needs `path:line` and blocks the merge.

## Terraform
- [ ] Remote state, never local{{#if infra.tf_state_bucket}} (`{{ infra.tf_state_bucket }}`){{/if}}
- [ ] No hardcoded account IDs or regions (data sources / variables)
- [ ] Standard tags on every new resource
- [ ] No wildcard IAM actions or resources in production policies
- [ ] Existing modules reused; no duplicate resources
- [ ] Persistent resources still have `prevent_destroy`
- [ ] `terraform fmt -check` and `terraform validate` pass; plan reviewed for destroys
- [ ] No state, tfvars or key files committed

## Kubernetes / Helm
- [ ] requests **and** limits, liveness **and** readiness probes on every container
- [ ] Images pinned to digest/SHA; no `:latest`
- [ ] No secrets in ConfigMaps or values files{{#if infra.vault}} (Vault only){{/if}}
- [ ] Correct namespaces (app: `{{ infra.namespace }}`); never `default`
- [ ] Non-root security context; PDB when replicas > 1
- [ ] `helm lint` / `kubeconform` output included
{{#if infra.argocd}}- [ ] Nothing managed by both ArgoCD and a pipeline Helm/kubectl step
{{/if}}
## CI/CD
- [ ] OIDC roles: read-only `{{ infra.plan_role_variable }}` for plans, `{{ infra.deploy_role_variable }}`
      only inside the `{{ infra.environment }}` environment; no long-lived cloud keys
- [ ] Every action pinned to a commit SHA
- [ ] Least-privilege `permissions:`
- [ ] Order: tests → Terraform → platform → build → scan → deploy
- [ ] Scan fails on CRITICAL/HIGH
- [ ] Production behind the `{{ infra.environment }}` environment; deploy `concurrency` set
- [ ] No untrusted `${{ github.event.* }}` text interpolated into `run:`
- [ ] Destroy workflow: `workflow_dispatch` only, typed confirmation unchanged

## Containers
- [ ] Multi-stage build; pinned base images; non-root final stage; no secrets in ARG/ENV

## General
- [ ] One concern per change; nothing outside the declared scope
- [ ] CLAUDE.md updated for new secrets, services or patterns

## Output
```
## Infra change review
### Terraform
✅ remote state
❌ missing standard tags on aws_security_group.app ({{ infra.iac_dir }}/modules/app/main.tf:44)
⏭ IAM: no policy changes
...
### Verdict
BLOCKED — fix ❌ items before merge.   |   APPROVED — all applicable checks pass.
```
